description:
In repos/activity-api/src/routes/activities.ts, the conservation-audit-emit route's internal read of its own audit endpoint is rejected with HTTP 401 because it sends no credentials; add the API key it already reads for the gap write.

The route calls its own conservation-audit endpoint over HTTP, but activity-api's auth middleware rejects that self-call because the fetch carries no Authorization header. The route already reads the key from the environment lower down for the gap-emit fetch; the read simply needs to move above the audit fetch and be applied to it.

Replace these three consecutive lines:
    const auditRes = await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:8080/v2/activities/conservation-audit?invariant=all', {
      signal: AbortSignal.timeout(30000),
    }).catch(() => null);

with exactly these lines:
    const selfKey = process.env['METABOB_API_KEY'] ?? '';
    const auditRes = await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:8080/v2/activities/conservation-audit?invariant=all', {
      headers: selfKey ? { Authorization: `ApiKey ${selfKey}` } : {},
      signal: AbortSignal.timeout(30000),
    }).catch(() => null);

This authenticates the self-call with the same key the route already uses for emitting gaps. Nothing else changes; the later read of the key for the gap-emit fetch remains as it is.

One replacement, one file. Change nothing else.

